# Tabs Styling & Layout

Tab components ship with minimal structural CSS so you can style them with regular CSS or Tailwind while keeping built-in layout, drag reordering, animations, and responsive shrinking.

## Orientation

Switch `<TabBar>` between horizontal and vertical layouts with the `orientation` prop (`"horizontal"` by default):

```svelte
<TabBar class="tab-bar" orientation="vertical">
  <Tab class="tab">
    <TabFavicon class="favicon">🌐</TabFavicon>
    <TabTitle class="title"/>
    <TabClose class="close">✕</TabClose>
  </Tab>
  <NewTab class="new-tab">+</NewTab>
</TabBar>
```

* **Horizontal mode:** Tabs sit in a single scrollable flex strip. Pinned tabs shrink to compact icon-only tiles on the left and wheel scrolling scrolls horizontally.
* **Vertical mode:** Pinned tabs render in a responsive grid at the top of the sidebar (`repeat(auto-fit, minmax(1.875rem, 1fr))`) that stretches across a single row when few tabs are pinned and wraps into square icon tiles as more are added. Unpinned tabs stack in a scrollable list below.

## Interactions

* **Drag reordering:** Drag unpinned tabs along the main axis or drag pinned tiles in 2D inside the vertical grid.
* **Middle-click:** Closes the clicked tab.
* **Keyboard navigation:** Supports arrow keys (`ArrowLeft`/`ArrowRight` in horizontal mode, `ArrowUp`/`ArrowDown` in vertical mode, plus `ArrowLeft`/`ArrowRight` across vertical pinned tiles), `Home`, `End`, `Enter`, and `Space`.
* **Compact tabs:** Container queries automatically hide inactive close buttons on narrow horizontal tabs and swap the icon for the close button on hover when very narrow.

## Data Attributes

Use these selectors to style states without fighting component specificity:

| Selector | Element | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `[data-orientation="horizontal" \| "vertical"]` | `TabBar` | Active tab bar orientation. |
| `[data-active]` | `Tab` | Currently selected tab. |
| `[data-pinned]` | `Tab` | Pinned tab (title and close button are hidden automatically). |
| `[data-dragging]` | `Tab` | Tab currently being dragged. |
| `[data-tab-title]` | `TabTitle` | Tab title text element. |
| `[data-tab-close]` | `TabClose` | Tab close button element. |
| `[data-tab-pinned]` | Internal grid | Pinned tab container (override `grid-template-columns` to customize vertical grid sizing). |
| `[data-tab-track]` | Internal list | Scrollable unpinned tab container in vertical mode. |


## Styling Example

```css
.tab-bar[data-orientation="vertical"] .tab[data-pinned] {
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
}
```